{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"list","title":"List","group":"","order":3,"html":"<p>collection of items in array data strucuture, in which collections are in heterogenous</p>\n<p>list = [ 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 ]</p>\n<p>index = [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 ]</p>\n<p>-ve index = [ -1, -2, -3, -4, -5 ]</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nprint(l)\nprint(l[0])\nprint(l[3])\nprint(l[-1])\nprint(l[-3])</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nl.append(30)\nprint(l)\nl.insert(1, 60)\nprint(l)\nprint(60 in l)\nprint(l.count(30))\nprint(l)\nprint(l.index(30))\nprint(l.index(30, 4, 7))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nl.remove(30)\nprint(l)\nprint(l.pop())\nprint(l)\nprint(l.pop(2))\nprint(l)\ndel l[1]\nprint(l)\ndel l[0:2]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nprint(min(l))\nprint(max(l))\nprint(sum(l))\nl.reverse()\nprint(l)\nl.sort()\nprint(l)\n\n# If list contain any other string than int, then the code will not work</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Working of list in Python</h3>\n<p>Basically list underlying the array data structure where contiguous memory location happens.</p>\n<p>It means there is a pre-allocated extra space for future additions.</p>\n<p>index = 0, 1, 2, 3, .....</p>\n<p>values = 2, 'p', '1', 'True' .....</p>\n<p>Advantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Random Access - easily get item in constant time</li>\n<li>cache friendly - locality of reference</li>\n<li>when we search for one data point it also store the reference of others if we have contiguous allocation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Disadvantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Insertion, Deletion, Search are slower because if any item added, deleted then we need to change the index position and move</li>\n</ul>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>How doe Dynamic size work...?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>pre allocate some extra space</li>\n<li>If it becomes full, do the following</li>\n</ul>\n<p> 1. Allocate a new space of larger size (multply by size of list * 2)</p>\n<p> 2. copy old space to new</p>\n<p> 3. Freeup the old space</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p>Explanation:</p>\n</div>\n<p>list = []</p>\n<p>for i in range(1, 1001):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>l.append(i)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Assumption :</p>\n<p>1. initially space for 10 items or allocated</p>\n<p>2. when a number is inserted at 11th index then block of '10' will be deallocated and then allocates double sized</p>\n<p>Time Complexity : O(1) # constant which is Amortized Time</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Average or Mean of a list</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 30, 40]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 25.0</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10,20,30,40]\ndef avg(l):\n  sum = 0\n  for i in l:\n    sum += i\n  n = len(l)\n  return sum/n\n\nprint(avg(l))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Seperate Even and Odd</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]<br><strong>Output:</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p>even = [10, 20, 40]</p>\n<p>odd = [11, 15, 19]</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def getevenodd(l):\n  even = []\n  odd = []\n  for i in l:\n    if i%2 == 0:\n      even.append(i)\n    else:\n      odd.append(i)\n  return even, odd\n\nl = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\neven, odd = getevenodd(l)\nprint(even)\nprint(odd)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Get Smaller Elements</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19], x = 21<br><strong>Output:</strong> [10, 20, 11, 15, 19]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def getSmaller(x):\n  res = []\n  for e in l:\n    if e &lt; x:\n      res.append(e)\n  return res\n\nl = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\nx = 21\nprint(getSmaller(x))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Slicing (List, Tuple and String)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Slicing\n\nl = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\nprint(l[0:5])\nprint(l[0:5:2])\nprint(l[:])\nprint(l[3:])\nprint(l[:3])\nprint(l[::-1])   # Reverse</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\ndup = l[:]\nprint(dup)\nprint(l)\nprint(l in dup)\nprint(dup is l)\n\n# False Because dup is separate in terms of memory allocation</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>t1 = (10, 20, 30)\nt2 = (10, 20, 30)\nprint(t1 is t2)\nprint(t1 == t2)\nprint(t1 in t2)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Comprehensions</h3>\n<p>List comprehension provides a shortcut syntax to create a list from another iterable.</p>\n<p>Iterable : A range function numbers are iterables</p>\n<p>syntax : list = [ item for item in collection if condition ]</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [ x for x in range(11)]\nprint(l)\n\nl = [ i for i in range(11) if i%2 == 0]\nprint(l)\n\nl = [ x for x in range(11) if x%2 == 1]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Get Smaller\n\ndef getSmaller(x):\n  return [e for e in l if e &lt; x]\n\nl = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\nx = 21\nprint(getSmaller(x))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Get Even Odd\n\ndef getEvenOdd(l):\n  even = [i for i in l if i%2 == 0]\n  odd = [i for i in l if i%2 == 1]\n  return even, odd\n\nl = [10, 20, 11, 40, 15, 19]\neven, odd = getEvenOdd(l)\nprint(even)\nprint(odd)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = \"ThrishankKuntimaddi\"\nl = [ch for ch in s if ch in 'aeiou']\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = ['Thrishank', 'Kuntimaddi', 'ThrishankKuntimaddi', 'Nani']\nl = [name for name in s if name.startswith(\"T\")]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l = [x*x for x in range(11)]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = ['Thrishank', 'Kuntimaddi', 'ThrishankKuntimaddi', 'Nani']\nl = [name.lower() for name in s if name.startswith(\"T\")]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Set Comprehension\nl = {x for x in range(11)}\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Dictionary Comprehension\nl = {x:x*2 for x in range(11)}\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>l1 = [10, 20, 30]\nl2 = ['a', 'b', 'c']\n\nd = dict(zip(l1, l2))\nprint(d)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Largest Element in a List</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 5, 20, 8]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 20</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\nl = [10, 2, 5, 8, 20, 19]\n\ndef getmax(l):\n  for x in l:\n    for y in l:\n      if y &lt; x:\n        break\n    else:\n      return x\n  return None\n\nprint(getmax(l))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef getmax(l):\n  if not l:\n    return None\n  else:\n    res = l[0]\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n      if l[i] &gt; res:\n        res = l[i]\n    return res\n\nprint(getmax(l))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Second Largest Element in a List</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 4, 5, 6, 1]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 10</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def secondLargest(l):\n  if len(l) &lt;= 1:\n    return None\n\n  lar = getMax(l)\n  slar = None\n\n  for x in l:\n    if x != lar:\n      if slar == None:\n        slar = x\n      else:\n        slar = max(slar,x)\n  return slar\n\ndef getMax(l):\n  res = l[0]\n  for i in range(1, len(l)):\n    res = max(res, l[i])\n  return res\n\n\nl = [10, 20, 4, 5, 6, 1]\nprint(secondLargest(l))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef secondLargest(l):\n  if len(l) &lt;= 1:\n    return None\n  lar = l[0]\n  slar = None\n  for x in l[1:]:\n    if x &gt; lar:\n      slar = lar\n      lar = x\n    elif x != lar:\n      if slar == None or slar &lt; x:\n        slar = x\n  return slar\n\nl = [10, 20, 4, 5, 6, 1]\nprint(secondLargest(l))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check if a List is sorted</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 30]<br><strong>Output:</strong> Yes</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef isSorted(l):\n  copy = sorted(l)\n  if copy == l:\n    return True\n  else:\n    return False\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nprint(isSorted(l))\n\nl = [29, 24, 32]\nprint(isSorted(l))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef ifSort(l):\n  i = 1\n  while i &lt; len(l):\n    if l[i] &lt; l[i-1]:\n      return False\n    i += 1\n  return True\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nprint(ifSort(l))\n\nl = [29, 24, 32]\nprint(ifSort(l))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Reverse of a List</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 30, 40]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [40, 30, 20, 10]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nl.reverse()\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nprint(l[::-1])</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 3\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nres = []\nfor i in range(len(l)-1, -1, -1):\n  res.append(l[i])\nprint(res)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 4\n\nl = [10, 20, 30]\nres = list(reversed(l))\nprint(res)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Reduce half Time\n\ndef reverse(l):\n  s = 0\n  e = len(l) - 1\n  while s &lt; e:\n    l[s], l[e] = l[e], l[s]\n    s += 1\n    e -= 1\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nreverse(l)\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Remove Duplicates from a sorted Array list</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 20, 30, 30, 30, 30}</p>\n</div>\n<p> size = 7</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 30, _, _, _, _ }</p>\n</div>\n<p> size = 3</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef remdup(arr, n):\n  temp = [0] * n\n  temp[0] = arr[0]\n  res = 1\n  for i in range(1, n):\n    if temp[res-1] != arr[i]:\n      temp[res] = arr[i]\n      res += 1\n  return res, temp\n\narr = [10, 20, 20, 30, 30, 30, 30]\nn = len(arr)\nno, temp = remdup(arr, n)\nprint(temp)\nprint(\"size : \", no)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef remdup(arr, n):\n  arr.sort()\n  res = 1\n  for i in range(1, n):\n    if arr[i] != arr[res-1]:\n      arr[res] = arr[i]\n      res += 1\n  return res\n\nl = [10, 20, 20, 30, 40, 30, 30]\nn = len(l)\nprint(remdup(l, n))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Left Rotate (Counter Clockwise) by One</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 30, 40]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [20, 30, 40, 10]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nl = l[1:] + l[0:1]\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nl.append(l.pop(0))\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Own Logic\n\ndef rotateByOne(l):\n  n = len(l)\n  x = l[0]\n  for i in range(1, n):\n    l[i-1] = l[i]\n  l[n-1] = x\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\nrotateByOne(l)\nprint(l)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Chicken Leg\n\ndef farn(T, cases):\n\n    for i in range(T):\n        X, Y, Z = cases[i]\n        chickens = (Z % X == 0)\n        ducks = (Z % Y == 0)\n\n        if chickens and ducks:\n            print(\"Any\")\n        elif chickens:\n            print(\"Chicken\")\n        elif ducks:\n            print(\"Duck\")\n        else:\n            print(\"Null\")\n\nT = int(input(\"Cases : \"))\nstack = []\n\nfor i in range(T):\n    X, Y, Z = map(int, input().strip().split())\n    stack.append([X, Y, Z])\n\nprint(stack)\n\nresults = farn(T, stack)</code></pre></figure></section>"}